{
  name: ccc
  testpoints:
  [
    {
      name: ccc
      desc:
        '''
        Instructs the ccc module to begin servicing GETSTATUS CCC. Feeds
        data bytes and bits to the module via its bus_tx/bus_rx interfaces
        to mimic actual I3C transaction. Checks if data bytes received
        correspond to correct GETSTATUS CCC response.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_ending_contract
      desc:
        '''
        Checks legal broadcast Sr release and directed addressed continuation.
        Holds command-valid through release, verifies context retirement, and
        checks STOP priority at command, defining-byte, defining-byte T-bit,
        payload-byte, payload T-bit, and completed-command checkpoints.
        Retains bad-parity payload T-bit collisions and adds valid-parity final
        payload T-bit collisions for both broadcast and directed SETMWL.
        Primes MWL to 0x3400, then collides STOP with byte 0x12's correct T=1;
        checks suppressed data-valid, unchanged MWL, and no immediate or delayed
        MWL update strobe while retiring the command.
        TE2 parity errors ignore subsequent traffic until STOP. Invalid
        premature Sr recovery is not implemented or required by this test.
        Requires the TE2 pulse, no further TE2 events or field effects while
        quiescent, and MWL/MRL/IBIL/reset-related signals unchanged from their
        post-error snapshot. Only MWL is explicitly programmed beforehand.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_ending_contract"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: next_ccc_command_retirement
      desc:
        '''
        Dedicated test_ccc.py check compares STOP with Sr+7E/W
        after GETBCR. Holds the parent's old command-valid through release.
        Runs through the test_ccc module in the nox ccc_verify session.
        Combinational handoff emits CccDone on STOP and CccNextCmd on the
        terminating 7E/W ACK completion.
        Both must clear command_code and command_code_valid on the release edge
        and leave them cleared while the main FSM owns the interface.
        '''
      tests: ["next_ccc_command_retirement"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: next_ccc_functional_chain
      desc:
        '''
        Dedicated functional control in test_ccc.py sends GETBCR,
        Sr+7E/W, then GETDCR without STOP. Checks exact, distinct response bytes
        and commands with opposite parity. Separately checks quiet CCC requests
        while the main FSM receives the new opcode. Does not assert internal
        command retirement, so a cleanup-contract failure is not mistaken for
        an externally observable command-chaining failure.
        '''
      tests: ["next_ccc_functional_chain"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_complete_handoff
      desc:
        '''
        All ownership-return paths emit a combinational CccDone, CccResumeAddr,
        or CccNextCmd action and return directly to WaitCCC. Covers STOP, broadcast Sr
        after both payload-bearing SETMWL and defining-byte-only RSTACT,
        direct-command chaining, command parity error, HDR entry, and TE0.
        Checks action timing on the event edge, retirement with held command-valid,
        and no release before the terminating ACK completes. Crosses every exit
        cause with simultaneous STOP and verifies suppression of normal field
        side effects. Idle bus events emit no handoff; STOP on initial command
        handoff completes immediately. Reset leaves no stale action.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_complete_handoff"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_mrl_capability_snapshot
      desc:
        '''
        Crosses main/virtual BCR[2] with broadcast and directed SETMRL and
        directed GETMRL. Changes live capability after sampling. Checks exact
        two-/three-byte counts, MRL/IBIL effects, ignored extension bytes, and
        fresh capability capture for each addressed GETMRL segment.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_mrl_capability_snapshot"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_rstact_target_ack
      desc:
        '''
        Crosses RSTACT defining bytes 0x01, 0x04, and unsupported 0x7F with no
        target, unknown-target write, main/virtual writes, and main-target read.
        Virtual-target reads are not exercised. The reserved 7E/W ACK
        retires decoding context without changing reset arming or the VT flag.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_rstact_target_ack"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_rstact_consumption
      desc:
        '''
        Local interface-driven NO_RESET consumption contract, broadcast/direct
        crossed with in-frame and STOP-before-first-detection sequences.
        C16-P1 checks armed NO_RESET and no reset request at first detection.
        C16-S checks arm/action retirement on the consuming edge.
        C16-P2 requires default peripheral request without escalation at a
        second detection, with no intervening normal START/SCL-fall or rearm.
        All checkpoints are retained before final failure. Bus-pattern detection
        and the rearm/START/VT controls are in ccc_rstact_pattern_consumption.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_rstact_consumption"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_rstact_consumption_requests
      desc:
        '''
        Crosses configured peripheral and whole-target resets with broadcast,
        main and virtual addressing, and simultaneous peripheral acknowledgement.
        Checks immediate arm/action/valid retirement while the selected request
        remains asserted, with request-set priority over acknowledgement.
        The independent VT flag survives consumption and acknowledgement.
        Subsequent raw detections use default peripheral reset, then escalation,
        without a normal START, rearm or external reset between patterns.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_rstact_consumption_requests"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
    {
      name: ccc_getstatus_segment_completion
      desc:
        '''
        GETSTATUS success pulses exactly at each addressed read's final T-bit,
        not again at STOP or a new CCC. A controller read-abort must not pulse
        success. Checks both simultaneous and delayed bus-monitor Sr after the
        TX abort indication, followed by a correctly received reserved header.
        Includes an interface-injected simultaneous final-T-bit-done/STOP
        collision: STOP suppresses success, unlike the non-STOP completion
        control. This is not claimed as a reachable legal-bus collision.
        '''
      tests: ["ccc_getstatus_segment_completion"]
      tags: ["ccc"]
    }
  ]
}